---
layout: layout.html
title: Contact
subtitle: Reach out for collabs, recommendations, or a quick hello from the road
eyebrow: Form and contact UI
intro: A styled contact section that adds another concrete frontend example to the app without needing backend infrastructure.
pageClass: contact-page
---
<section class="contactLayout">
    <div class="contactIntro">
        <span class="sectionTag">Get in touch</span>
        <h2>For brand partnerships, queer travel questions, or itinerary swaps.</h2>
        <p>We are most interested in practical travel collaborations, community recommendations, and projects that align with affordable, inclusive travel.</p>
        <div class="contactList">
            <div>
                <strong>Email</strong>
                <span>hello@mrsandmrsmaps.com</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <strong>Base</strong>
                <span>Madrid, Spain</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <strong>Best for</strong>
                <span>Editorial features, travel notes, and queer-friendly destination research</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <form class="contactForm">
        <label>
            Name
            <input type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your name">
        </label>
        <label>
            Email
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="name@example.com">
        </label>
        <label>
            Topic
            <select name="topic">
                <option>Collaboration</option>
                <option>Travel question</option>
                <option>General hello</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <label>
            Message
            <textarea name="message" rows="6" placeholder="Tell us where you're headed or what you're working on."></textarea>
        </label>
        <button type="button">Send message</button>
    </form>
</section>
